Recommended action: The patient should receive prompt medical assessment. If an allergic reaction is suspected, further doses should not be taken until a healthcare professional advises on safe treatment. Difficulty breathing, swelling of the face or tongue, or fainting requires emergency medical attention. The suspected reaction should be documented and reported through the appropriate pharmacovigilance channel.

